it was an effort created to help some  local residents who were struggling with  poverty during the pandemic  and today delivering with dignity  celebrated its one year anniversary  helping the community while also keeping  dozens of employees working  christian casares joining us in the  studio with more on the effort that has  really come a long way in the past year  that's right denise will delivering with  dignity started a year ago today as an  emergency response to the pandemic  they started delivering 3 500 meals  weekly and today  that number has almost doubled to 6 500  meals  every single week now the program works  with 50  non-profit groups to help identify  county residents who are struggling with  food and are at high risk of covet 19  when they step away from their home this  includes elderly folks people with  underlying medical conditions and  family members living in the same home  now the concept also helps keep  restaurant employees working  since they prepare the meals now for  locally independent uh owned businesses  who pack the meals are delivered by  volunteers to people's home  honeysuckle owner elizabeth blau says  the effort has provided critical support  to many restaurants struggling to keep  their doors open  this was a unique idea because we needed  to get these meals directly  to people's homes because community  centers and schools and senior centers  were closed and so those normal  distribution channels  became very very challenging to to  people  listen to this more than 325 000 meals  have been delivered since the program  launched  last march now they have reached almost  every single zip code here in southern  nevada  nearly 50 percent of those homes are  senior citizens  and 15 percent of them have children now  several donations  have kept the program going and allowing  them to expand to northern nevada very  soon now there are still  many people struggling to get food on  their table so if you wish to help make  a donation or become a volunteer  visit eightnewsnow.com for all those  details christian concedes 8 news now
 

